{"id": "EUVD-2026-94305", "enisaUuid": "7364790b-2e24-3b49-a51e-2d7e4893051c", "description": "patool before 4.0.6 contains an OS command injection vulnerability on Windows because shell_quote_nt fails to escape cmd.exe metacharacters or embedded double quotes in archive filenames. Attackers can supply crafted filenames like report&calc.gz for single-file formats run with shell=True to execute commands with patool process privileges.", "datePublished": "2026-10-07T11:59:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-07T14:43:03", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/wummel/patool/commit/592f35761f428afbcde2888ecd3cc4af43881aeb", "https://github.com/wummel/patool", "https://github.com/wummel/patool/blob/4.0.5/patoolib/util.py#L110-L116", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/patool-before-4.0.6-os-command-injection-on-windows-via-shell-quote-nt"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-106057", "GHSA-73h5-w67h-9rfh"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.76, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2b424407-19c7-3ba1-aa84-fc2a09d6f895", "product": {"name": "patool", "vendor": {"name": "wummel"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.0.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0b4378a3-70d1-3cae-949d-e5121f49f56c", "vendor": {"name": "wummel"}}], "isExploited": false}